

   =====( Conf V1.00 )=========================================


           Trion Conference CliDoor.

           (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

           Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   Conf is the Trion BBS system conference system.

   With this door users on different BBS nodes can chat with each
   other .. up to 10 users can use it at the same time.
   (the same amount of BBS Nodes there can be run at this moment)
   Up to 10 different conferences can be entered.


   If the user enters the door he sees a prompt where he can type
   text or commands .. the text is displayed on the screen and
   is send to all other conference doors.

   There are 4 commands the user can use on the prompt, after
   the "/name" and "/conf" command the user will be prompted
   for input.
   These are all the commands with a little explanation:   


   /quit
            This will exit the door.

   /name
            With this command users can choose an other name
            so they can use aliases.

   /cls
            To clear the text window.

   /conf
            To change to an other conference.
            When a number of users are chatting with each other
            there is a possibilty that they not all want to chat
            about the same thing .. so there are a number of 
            conferences .. only the people who are in the same
            conference can read each others writings.
            Every user who enters the conference door starts in
            conference 0, with the /conf the user can go to
            an other conference. There are 10 conferences (0-9).
            At the top of the screen is the conference this user is
            in. At the rigth of that is a display where you can see
            how many users use the conference door and in which
            conference they are. Every place corresponds with
            a BBS node. The first place with node 0, and the last
            place with node 9.
            A '.' means there is no user in the conference door at
            that node.
            A '*' is the node of the user in this node.
            A number is the conference all other nodes are in.



   Note that when you enter the door there is a message send
   to all other BBS nodes that some one has entered the conference
   including the name of the user on the node.



   The door is started by adding something like this to your menus:



Cmd "C" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "tron:doors/conf/conf '~200' ~50"
EndCmd



   The "C" part is command which is used to start at and can be
   changed to suit your menus.
   The '~200' is a tilde code to get the name of the user to the
   door .. the '' are needed .. because they are translated into
   "" which in their turn are needed in case there are spaces
   in the name of the User.
   The ~50 is the tilde code for the BBS node number the door
   was started on .. node that this is an older door .. the
   newer doors only require the ~50 part .. and they can then
   ask the Username from the BBS node.


   Note: there is a tiny problem with conf .. if two users send
   lines to each other at exactly the same moment the programmas
   halt because they are waiting on each other but this is very rare.


